libass: no clang-cl flag for qcc.

0.17.5 tries /clang:-fno-math-errno (clang-cl's spelling). qcc takes the
unknown argument for a file and hands it to the linker, so the compile-only
flag check succeeds and every link check after it fails ("Unable to locate
math functions!"). Try it only where the compiler can be MSVC-like.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -53,7 +53,10 @@
 # Configure Compiler
 ## Perf tuning features
 AX_APPEND_COMPILE_FLAGS([-fno-math-errno])
-AX_APPEND_COMPILE_FLAGS([/clang:-fno-math-errno])
+dnl clang-cl's spelling. qcc passes an argument it does not know (a path, to
+dnl it) on to the linker, so the compile-only check "accepts" it and every
+dnl link test after it fails: only where the compiler is MSVC-like.
+AS_CASE([$host_os], [mingw*|cygwin*|windows*], [AX_APPEND_COMPILE_FLAGS([/clang:-fno-math-errno])])
 
 ## Warnings
 AX_APPEND_COMPILE_FLAGS([ \
